1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,972
Your SIP isn't broken.

2
00:00:01,992 --> 00:00:03,510
It's just early.

3
00:00:03,530 --> 00:00:05,142
Say you invest five thousand

4
00:00:05,162 --> 00:00:06,325
rupees a month.

5
00:00:06,345 --> 00:00:07,369
After five years,

6
00:00:07,389 --> 00:00:08,882
you've put in three lakh.

7
00:00:08,902 --> 00:00:10,500
It's worth about four lakh.

8
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:11,499
Feels slow.

9
00:00:11,519 --> 00:00:12,495
After ten years:

10
00:00:12,515 --> 00:00:13,282
six lakh in.

11
00:00:13,302 --> 00:00:14,804
About eleven and a half

12
00:00:14,824 --> 00:00:15,439
lakh.

13
00:00:15,459 --> 00:00:16,638
After twenty years:

14
00:00:16,658 --> 00:00:17,620
twelve lakh in.

15
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,030
About fifty lakh.

16
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:19,730
Same SIP.

17
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,621
Same amount.

18
00:00:20,641 --> 00:00:22,530
The growth just shows up

19
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:23,232
late.

20
00:00:23,252 --> 00:00:24,329
That's compounding.

21
00:00:24,349 --> 00:00:26,029
Your returns start earning

22
00:00:26,049 --> 00:00:27,501
their own returns.

23
00:00:27,521 --> 00:00:28,940
And most people quit in

24
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:29,586
year three,

25
00:00:29,606 --> 00:00:31,594
right before the curve bends.

26
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:33,366
This assumes twelve percent

27
00:00:33,386 --> 00:00:33,865
a year.

28
00:00:33,885 --> 00:00:35,748
Real returns go up and down,

29
00:00:35,768 --> 00:00:37,730
and nothing is guaranteed.

30
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,370
So don't judge your SIP

31
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:40,248
by year one.

32
00:00:40,268 --> 00:00:42,783
Judge it by year fifteen.
